<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emmanuel Macron</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1977</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emmanuel Macron is a French politician who was elected President of the French Fifth Republic in 2017 at the age of 39, having founded the centrist movement En <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marche</a> the year before. He was re-elected in 2022. His presidency saw labour and pension reforms, the gilets jaunes protests and a strong emphasis on European integration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emmanuel-macron.jpg" alt="Emmanuel Macron" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nebojša Tejić · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emmanuel_Macron_2025_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
